The one point that no one else has yet mentioned is that poison
resistance and food poisoning are completely separate.  Food poisoning
is a misnomer for a bacterial infection caused by ingesting tainted
meat.  There is no nethack resistance for this other than not eating
the corpses of the undead (or are you resistant to food poisoning if
you are poly'd into an undead?)...  Poison resistance covers all other
instances of "poisoning" in nethack.  There are, much later on,
instances of monsters making you deathly ill, for which, again, there
are no normal resistances, only cures.

